[38;2;124;124;124m- The topology on $\mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R})$: This is the strong dual topology [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mof $\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R})$ (smooth functions with the $C^\infty$ topology). [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mConvergence $f_n \to f$ in $\mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R})$ means $\langle f_n, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\varphi \rangle \to \langle f, \varphi \rangle$ for all $\varphi \in \mathcal{E}[0m[38;2;124;124;124m(\mathbb{R})$ (weak-* convergence), or equivalently uniform convergence on [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mbounded subsets of $\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R})$ (strong convergence). Actually, for[0m[38;2;124;124;124msequences, weak-* convergence and strong convergence coincide in $\mathcal{E}'$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mby the Banach-Steinhaus theorem (since $\mathcal{E}$ is a Fréchet space, hence [0m
